            <ArticleTitle>[Management of coronary heart disease: seasonal features].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>21-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Atenolol was tested for its effect on the fatty acid spectrum of serum low-density lipoproteins in patients with coronary heart disease in winter and summer. There was a significant increase in saturated fatty acids and a reduction in unsaturated fatty acids during treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
